Release Notes STM32MP1 OpenSTLinux BSP:
=======================================

BSP-Yocto-OpenSTLinux-STM32MP1-PD20.1.0  2020-09-18
===================================================
- Linux ST Vendor Kernel v4.19.94
- U-boot ST Vendor v2018.11
- TF-A ST Vendor v2.0
- Linux integration OpenSTLinux v1.2.0 (openstlinux-20-02-19):

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- st-image-weston (DISTRO=openstlinux-weston) on:
  * phycore-stm32mp1-1
  * phycore-stm32mp1-2
  * phycore-stm32mp1-3

- st-image-core (DISTRO=openstlinux-eglfs) on:
  * phycore-stm32mp1-1
  * phycore-stm32mp1-2
  * phycore-stm32mp1-3
  * phycore-stm32mp1-6

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 16.04 64-bit

Features:
---------
- Added support for new machine:
  * phycore-stm32mp1-2 (phyCORE-STM32MP1 ALPHA2-Kit Dev Board, stm32mp157aac @650Mhz MPU (old rev), 3D GPU, 1GiB RAM, 8GiB eMMC)
  * phycore-stm32mp1-3 (phyCORE-STM32MP1 phyBOARD-Sargas full-featured, stm32mp157cac @650Mhz MPU, 3D GPU, 1GiB RAM, 8GiB eMMC, 16MB QSPI NOR)
  * phycore-stm32mp1-4 (phyCORE-STM32MP1 phyBOARD-Sargas full-featured, stm32mp157fac @800Mhz MPU, 3D GPU, 1GiB RAM, 8GiB eMMC, 16MB QSPI NOR)
  * phycore-stm32mp1-5 (phyCORE-STM32MP1 phyBOARD-Sargas full featured, stm32mp153aac @650Mhz MPU, no 3D GPU, 1GiB RAM, 8GiB eMMC)
  * phycore-stm32mp1-6 (phyCORE-STM32MP1 phyBOARD-Sargas low cost, stm32mp153aac @650Mhz MPU, no 3D GPU, 512MB RAM, 512MB NAND)
  * phycore-stm32mp1-7 (phyCORE-STM32mp1 phyBOARD-Sargas super low cost, stm32mp153aac @650Mhz MPU, no 3D GPU, 512MB RAM, 128MB NAND)

- Added new PHYTEC custom OpenSTLinux Distribution (DISTRO):
  * openstlinux-tiny:
    Created for SOM equipped with small Flash memory size (128MB).
    It is based on OpenSTLinux distro with the following differences:
      + no X11, no Wayland, no eglfs
      + no uninative support
      + SysVinit instead of systemd
      + following features removed: alsa, wifi, nfs, bluetooth, bluez5

- Added new PHYTEC custom OpenSTLinux BSP Image:
  * st-image-core-minimal (required DITRO=openstlinux-tiny):
    Image based on st-image-core, but without:
	  + display framework
      + tools framework for base components (core, kernel, network, audio, ui)
	  + package management system

  * st-example-image-qt-minimal (required DITRO=openstlinux-eglfs):
	Image based on 'st-example-image-qt' with fewer features and QT packages to decrease the image size


- Added new features:
  * Boot from eMMC
  * Boot from NAND
  * NAND support (u-boot/kernel)
  * PEB-AV-01 support (HDMI module)
  * PEB-AV-02 with AC158 EDT 7" capacitive touchcreen display support
  * PEB-WLBT-05 support (WLAN/Bluetooth expansion)
  * "RedBear IoT pHAT v1.0" support (WLAN/Bluetooth Raspberry Pi HAT solution)
  * Raspberry Pi 7" Touch Screen MIPI DSI Display support (touchcreen is not functionnal)

- Existing features (from ALPHA2 release):
  * Boot from SD-card
  * Boot from NOR (Linux running on eMMC)
  * NOR SPI suport (u-boot/kernel)
  * eMMC support (u-boot/kernel) - no direct boot from eMMC
  * SD-card support (u-boot/kernel
  * I2C support (u-boot/kernel)
  * UARTs support (u-boot/kernel)
  * RS485 support (kernel)
  * EEPROM support (u-boot/kernel)
  * USB-Host support (u-boot/kernel)
  * USB-OTG support (kernel)
  * Ethernet support - 100Mpbs/1Gbps (kernel) and 100Mbps (u-boot)
  * CAN FD support(kernel)
  * SPI support (kernel)
  * Audio support (Line IN/OUT, Headphone) (kernel)
  * RTC support (kernel)
  * LED dimmer(PCA9533/01 support (kernel)
  * User buttons support(kernel)
  * TIMERs (kernel)
  * ADCs (kernel)
  * PEB-AV-02 with AC158 screen support (touchscreen driver not loaded automatically at boot)
  * MB1407 MIPI DSI screen support (4" touch screen display from STMicroelectronics)

Known Issues/Limitations:
-------------------------
- PMIC buck4 regulator is not switched off in standby modes (workaround to the standby mode phyBOARD-Sargas Hardware reset issue)
- Ethernet support in u-boot is limited to 100Mbps
- From u-boot, there is no mechanism to update the BSP (from Network, SD-card, USB Flash Drive or USB DFU)
- Other Limitations: refer to https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu-ecosystem-v1/wiki/STM32MP15_OpenSTLinux_release_note
